MASTER DEVELOPMENT PROMPT — ENTERPRISE PAYMENT PROCESSOR / PAYMENT HUB

1. Project Overview

Design and develop an enterprise-grade, configurable Payment Processor Application for a global banking environment.

The Payment Processor will act as a centralized payment orchestration platform responsible for receiving payment instructions from various Product Processor Applications, validating and enriching payment data, applying configurable payment controls, transforming payment instructions into appropriate financial message formats, routing payments through configured gateways, receiving acknowledgements and credit confirmations, and publishing payment lifecycle events to downstream applications.

The platform must support global payments, cross-border payments, domestic payments, high-value payments, real-time payments, and multi-currency transactions.

The application must have a modern, responsive, enterprise banking UI for:

1. Payment Operations.
2. Payment Processing and Monitoring.
3. Payment Pipeline Configuration.
4. Payment Control Configuration.
5. Gateway and Connectivity Configuration.
6. Maker-Checker Approval.
7. Payment Repair and Exception Management.
8. Payment Reporting and Audit.

The application must be configuration-driven. Source systems, payment controls, message formats, routing rules, gateways, downstream applications, and operational approval workflows must not be hardcoded.

