2.2 Payment Processing Engine

Implement a centralized payment processing engine.

Processing flow:

1. Receive Payment Instruction.
2. Validate Source System.
3. Validate Payment Schema.
4. Normalize Payment Data.
5. Enrich Payment Data.
6. Retrieve SSI information.
7. Apply Payment Controls.
8. Perform Payment Risk Assessment.
9. Determine Payment Route.
10. Determine Message Format.
11. Transform Payment Message.
12. Apply Maker-Checker Approval if required.
13. Submit Payment to Gateway.
14. Receive Gateway Acknowledgement.
15. Receive Credit Confirmation.
16. Update Payment Lifecycle.
17. Publish Payment Events.
18. Generate Audit Records.

The processing engine must support synchronous and asynchronous processing.

Use configurable state transitions and prevent invalid payment lifecycle transitions.

