17. Mandatory Acceptance Criteria

The completed application must demonstrate the following end-to-end scenarios.

Scenario 1: Product Processor Payment

* Receive payment instruction from GCMS.
* Validate payment.
* Enrich payment.
* Execute configured controls.
* Transform to pacs.008.
* Route through BOX.
* Receive gateway acknowledgement.
* Receive credit confirmation.
* Publish downstream audit events.

Scenario 2: Financial Institution Payment

* Receive payment instruction.
* Apply controls.
* Transform to pacs.009.
* Route through CitiSwitch.
* Track payment lifecycle.

Scenario 3: Domestic Payment

* Receive payment instruction.
* Apply domestic controls.
* Transform to domestic format.
* Route through ISSAC.
* Receive acknowledgement and confirmation.

Scenario 4: Manual Payment

* Operations maker creates payment.
* Retrieve SSI from AMC.
* Enrich payment.
* Apply controls.
* Submit for maker-checker approval.
* Checker approves.
* Payment is processed and routed.

Scenario 5: Sanctions Hold

* Payment matches sanctions screening rule.
* Payment is held.
* Compliance user investigates.
* Authorized release or rejection.
* Audit trail generated.

Scenario 6: Duplicate Payment

* Duplicate payment is detected.
* Payment is placed on hold.
* Operations investigates.
* Authorized resolution is recorded.

Scenario 7: Dual-Blind Approval

* Payment requires two independent checkers.
* First checker approves.
* Second checker independently approves.
* Payment is released only after both approvals.

Scenario 8: Pipeline Configuration

* Maker creates a new pipeline.
* Configure source system.
* Configure controls.
* Configure pacs.008 message format.
* Configure BOX connectivity.
* Configure downstream audit events.
* Submit for checker approval.
* Activate the approved pipeline.

Scenario 9: Gateway Failure

* Gateway is unavailable.
* Payment follows configured retry and fallback routing rules.
* Operations can investigate the payment.
* No duplicate payment execution occurs.

Scenario 10: Payment Event Publication

* Payment lifecycle events are generated.
* Events are delivered to downstream applications.
* Failed delivery is retried.
* Event delivery status is visible to Operations.

